                                </p>

                                <p>
                                    This meant conducting interviews throughout
                                    the organization, annotating transcripts to
                                    pull out relevant details, and synthesizing
                                    everything into a comprehensive diagram. I
                                    also worked with researchers and designers
                                    to create usability studies using
                                    UserTesting.
                                </p>

                                <p>
                                    <strong>What I learned:</strong> The biggest takeaway
                                    from FM Global was that in UX, you have to work
                                    hard to define the problem before diving into
                                    solutions. The better you understand a problem,
                                    the better you can solve it. This taught me to
                                    slow down, do the research, and let the insights
                                    guide the design—not the other way around.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- UVU -->
                        <div class="mb-12">
